+# Local Base Fork
+
+This checkout can fork Base, but the onboarding note is wrong about the command and the sanity check.
+
+## What went wrong
+
+The note says:
+
+```bash
+yarn fork base
+```
+
+In this repo that does **not** pass `base` into the workspace fork script. A dry run through the actual script path shows what it starts:
+
+```bash
+$ MAKEFLAGS=-n yarn fork base
+anvil --fork-url mainnet --chain-id 31337
+```
+
+So the local node is a fork of Ethereum mainnet, not Base. Transactions still mine because Anvil is running, and `cast chain-id` still returns a number because the Makefile forces a local chain id for every fork:
+
+```makefile
+# packages/foundry/Makefile
+fork: setup-anvil-wallet
+	anvil --fork-url ${FORK_URL} --chain-id 31337
+```
+
+The default comes from the Foundry package script:
+
+```json
+// packages/foundry/package.json
+"fork": "make fork FORK_URL=${1:-mainnet}"
+```
+
+The root script only delegates to that workspace script:
+
+```json
+// package.json
+"fork": "yarn foundry:fork",
+"foundry:fork": "yarn workspace @se-2/foundry fork"
+```
+
+And the aliases are in `packages/foundry/foundry.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[rpc_endpoints]
+mainnet = "https://eth-mainnet.alchemyapi.io/v2/${ALCHEMY_API_KEY}"
+base = "https://mainnet.base.org"
+```
+
+That is why reads at Base USDC, `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`, come back empty under the bad command: the address has code on Base, but not on Ethereum mainnet.
+
+## Correct command
+
+From the repo root, pass the fork name through with `--`:
+
+```bash
+yarn fork -- base
+```
+
+A dry run confirms this reaches Anvil correctly:
+
+```bash
+$ MAKEFLAGS=-n yarn fork -- base
+anvil --fork-url base --chain-id 31337
+```
+
+Equivalent direct command:
+
+```bash
+cd packages/foundry
+make fork FORK_URL=base
+```
+
+## Better sanity check
+
+Do not use only `cast chain-id` against the local node. In this repo it returns `31337` for any fork because of `--chain-id 31337`.
+
+Use a Base-specific check instead. Since this project depends on Base USDC, verify that the local fork can read that contract:
+
+```bash
+cast call 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913 \
+  'symbol()(string)' \
+  --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545
+```
+
+Expected output on a Base fork:
+
+```text
+"USDC"
+```
+
+Optional Anvil-specific check:
+
+```bash
+cast rpc anvil_nodeInfo --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545
+```
+
+Look for:
+
+```json
+"forkConfig":{"forkUrl":"https://mainnet.base.org", ...}
+```

